course: dictionary
lesson: 10656
title: Unjust: not fair
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unjust means not fair or not right. Look at its parts: just means fair, and un- means not. So unjust is the opposite of just.
explain: We use unjust when someone is treated badly without a good reason. Look at the clues around the word. A punishment that is far too harsh for a small mistake is unjust.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «It is unjust that the youngest child was blamed for something her brother did» still makes sense with "not fair" in place of unjust, so you know you are right.
fact: Unjust means not fair or not right.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unjust is the opposite of just.
fact: «An unjust punishment» is one that is too harsh or given without a good reason.
fact: «Some laws have been truly unjust»: in 1955 Rosa Parks refused to give up her bus seat in Alabama, breaking an unfair law.
fact: Civil disobedience means breaking an unjust law peacefully to change it, and many people say it can be right.
exercise: «Civil disobedience means breaking an unjust law peacefully to change it.» Which word in this sentence means not fair? | *unjust | peacefully | law | breaking
exercise: «It is unjust that the youngest child was blamed for something her brother did.» What does unjust mean? | *Not fair | Very loud | Funny | Very kind
exercise: What is the opposite of unjust? | Unsafe | Unwell | *Just | Unkind
test: «Rosa Parks refused to give up her bus seat, breaking an unfair law.» What does unjust mean? | Very quick | Brand new | *Not fair or not right | Long and boring
test: Which word means the opposite of unjust? | Unwell | Unkind | *Just | Unsafe
exam: Maya says, «It is unjust that I had to stay in while my friends went out.» What does Maya mean? | *She thinks it is not fair | She wants to go out with her friends | She is pleased with her day | She is very tired
